      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T16:47:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In reviewing makeTextureImage Rob pointed out that isTextureBacked is ambiguous, and in fact in places we are depending on it meaning \"Ganesh backed\". So this removes the ambiguity.\n\nI\u0027m not tied to the names.",
      "revId": "36a039cf81b4195dbc64f648228c42c40968a913",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8eaf1913_0201e53b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T17:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m trying to imagine what clients want here, especially as we start to have Ganesh and Graphite in clients. Maybe there are uses where clients are doing different things with Graphite backed vs Ganesh backed textures. But I would also kind of hope they would already know that which of those GPU backends they were using and wouldn\u0027t need us to tell them via an SkImage. So I think it general clients will just want to know if an SkImage is a \"gpu\" texture image or not. Which makes me think we just want isTextureBacked which would return true for either Ganesh or Graphite. This also helps clients start to transfer over to only using texture backend SkImages in Ganesh and can use the same asserts later. ",
      "revId": "36a039cf81b4195dbc64f648228c42c40968a913",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f3235b1_2de1e787",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T18:51:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I can\u0027t find it right now, but there\u0027s at least one example in Chrome where they check for texture-backed for an sk_sp\u003cSkImage\u003e and then call a method that\u0027s only valid when used with Ganesh. We have examples like that in our test and sample code as well. \n\nIf you\u0027re working with only one backend I agree it would be okay. My concern is that as when we\u0027re making the transition from Ganesh to Graphite we could be in this hybrid mode where we don\u0027t know what\u0027s what\u0027s backing the SkImage, will call wrong methods, and that will lead to crashes. However, if we can be sure there will only be a GrDirectContext, or a Recorder, and not both, then maybe it\u0027s not much of a concern.\n\nI think ideally there would be:\n* isTextureBacked -- it\u0027s a GPU texture image\n* isGaneshBacked -- you can call GrDirectContext-based image calls on this\n* isGraphiteBacked -- you can call Recorder-based image calls on this\n\nBut isTextureBacked is in use out there already as the first two meanings.",
      "parentUuid": "8eaf1913_0201e53b",
      "revId": "36a039cf81b4195dbc64f648228c42c40968a913",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa58482d_7a735fbe",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T19:04:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess I would argue we should makes this API work as we would ideally want it to work. So if we want isTextureBackend to be its a gpu texture image (which I think we do), then we should update clients to behave in that way. Obviously right now there will be cases where a client (i.e. chrome) uses that function and calls ganesh only things after, but that is something we\u0027ll have to sort out during the transition.\n\nIf we don\u0027t have a strong reason where a client needs to branch on an SkImage know graphite or ganesh right now, I say let\u0027s wait until we have that reason to add these APIs.\n\nAlso FWIW if our transition works correctly, Chrome will always things they are in a graphite context. They don\u0027t explicitly need to know that ganesh sits under the API.\n\nOn a side note, I really really hope no client ever tries to have an active GrContext and skgpu::Context active at the same time....",
      "parentUuid": "0f3235b1_2de1e787",
      "revId": "36a039cf81b4195dbc64f648228c42c40968a913",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
